# Courier Performance Analytics – UI Implementation Rule

## Objective

Build the Courier Performance Analytics page at `/courier/performance` for the Ashraf Courier Business Platform.  
**Focus:** Pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern UI for individual courier performance metrics and insights.  
**No backend logic or API integration—use only static/mock data.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)

---

## 2. Page Structure & Features

### 2.1. Header

- **Title:** "Courier Performance Analytics"
- **Courier Info:** Avatar, name, courier ID, and current status badge

### 2.2. Key Metrics Overview

- **Delivery Completion Rate:** Percentage, with visual indicator (progress bar or radial chart)
- **Customer Ratings:** Average rating (stars), count, and recent feedback snippet
- **Earnings Breakdown:** Total earnings, breakdown by week/month, and payout status
- **Efficiency Metrics:** Average delivery time, distance per delivery, on-time rate

### 2.3. Performance Trends

- **Charts:** Line/bar charts for delivery completion, earnings, and efficiency over time (mock data)
- **Filters:** Date range picker (UI only, no backend)

### 2.4. Customer Feedback

- **Recent Feedback List:** Customer comments, ratings, and delivery references
- **Sentiment Indicator:** Positive/neutral/negative badge or icon

### 2.5. Accessibility & Responsiveness

- All elements must be keyboard navigable and screen-reader friendly
- Color contrast must meet WCAG AA
- Fully responsive: mobile, tablet, desktop

---

## 3. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication
- Use mock data for all metrics, charts, and feedback

---

## 4. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere
- Functional components only
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs
- Descriptive naming and clear structure
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible

---

## 5. Naming & Scoping

- **IDs:** Globally unique, format: `parcego-courier-performance-[purpose]-[unique]`
- **Classes:** BEM/SMACSS, prefix: `parcego-courier-performance__element--modifier`
- **Dynamic Elements:** Append unique hash/UUID for runtime-generated IDs/classes

---

## 6. UI/UX Patterns

- Use shadcn/ui components for all UI blocks
- Use Tailwind for all styling; no custom CSS unless necessary
- Apply premium transitions for interactive elements (hover, focus, entrance)
- Use subtle, modern effects (see premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc)
- No layout shifts or jank; use only `transform` and `opacity` for animations

---

## 7. Deliverables

- `/courier/performance` page and all required UI components
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend)
- README update with instructions for running the frontend demo

---

## 8. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by project lead

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Courier Performance Analytics UI, ready for future backend/API integration.

---